          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            is
            %em regular
            if it behaves like an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+epimorphism"} effective epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇒
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇔
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leftrightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+monomorphism"} effective monomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇒
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular monomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇔
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leftrightarrow
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding"} embedding
                \.
          %p
            The universal factorization through an embedding is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong regular monomorphism
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : c \to d
              in some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              which occurs as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of
              %em some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair+of+parallel+morphisms"} pair of parallel morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \stackrel{\to}{\to} e
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi d
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c \stackrel{f}{\to} d \stackrel{\longrightarrow}{\longrightarrow} e
            %p exists.
          %p
            From the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            it follows directly that a regular monomorphism is in particular a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            The dual concept is that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Beware that (
              %a{:href => "#CassidyHebertKelly"}> CassidyHebertKelly
              ) use ‘regular monomorphism’ in a more general way: for them, a regular monomorphism is by definition the joint equalizer of an arbitrary family of parallel pairs of morphisms with common domain. This concept is sometimes called
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monomorphism"} strict monomorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+epimorphism"} strict epimorphism
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_effective_monomorphisms Relation to effective monomorphisms
          #EffectiveMonomorphism.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to B
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+monomorphism"} effective monomorphism
              if it is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              of its
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel+pair"} cokernel pair
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %msub
                              %mo +
                              %mi A
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; \stackrel{i}{\to} &amp; B \\
                    i \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow i_1 \\
                    B &amp; \underset{i_2}{\to} &amp; B +_A B
                    }
            %p
              exists and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is the equalizer of the pair of coprojections
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %msub
                        %mo +
                        %mi A
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1, i_2: B \stackrel{\to}{\to} B +_A B
          #RegEquEff.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel+pairs"} cokernel pairs
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+monomorphism"} effective monomorphism
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EffectiveMonomorphism"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p It is clear that every effective monomorphism is regular, we need to show the converse.
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon A \to B
              is the equalizer of a pair of morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g: B \to C
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EffectiveMonomorphism"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: E \to B
              be the equalizer of the pair of coprojections
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1, i_2
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ i = g \circ i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo +
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: B +_A B \to C
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \circ i_1 = f
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \circ i_2 = g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f j = \phi i_1 j = \phi i_2 j = g j
            %p
              and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: A \to B
              is the equalizer of the pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, g)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k: E \to A
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi i
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j = i k
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1 i = i_2 i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l: A \to E
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi j
                      %mi l
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = j l
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l
              are mutually inverse.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                is regular. More generally, this holds in every
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adhesive+category"} adhesive category
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          #RegularMonomorphismsOfTopologicalSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (regular monomorphisms of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              In the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                  are the those
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                  which are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+functions"} injective functions
              %li
                %p
                  the regular monomorphisms are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+embeddings"} topological embeddings
                  (that is, the injective continuous functions whose sources have the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induced+topology"} topologies induced
                  from their targets); these are in fact all of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+monomorphisms"} extremal monomorphisms
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Regarding the first statement: an injective continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              clearly has the cancellation property that defines monomorphisms: for parallel continuous functions
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1,g_2 \colon Z \to X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ g_1 = f \circ g_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1 = g_2
              because continuous functions are equal precisely if their underlying functions of sets are equal. Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              has the cancellation property, then testing on points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1, g_2 \colon \ast \to X
              gives that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is injective.
            %p
              Regarding the second statement: from the construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizers"} equalizers
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              (
              %a{:href => "Top#EqualizerInTop"}> this example
              ) we have that these are topological subspace inclusions.
            %p
              Conversely, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon X \to Y
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace+embedding"} topological subspace embedding
            %p
              To that end, form the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel+pair"} cokernel pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i_1, i_2)
              by taking the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              against itself (in the category of sets, and using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topology"} quotient topology
              on a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union+space"} disjoint union space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RegEquEff"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              are regular, we get the function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              back and (again by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Top#EqualizerInTop"} this example
          #reg.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
          %p
            In contrast, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+monomorphisms"} normal monomorphisms
            (where one of the morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to e
            is required to be the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroups"} normal subgroups
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The elementary proof we give follows
              %a{:href => "http://katmat.math.uni-bremen.de/acc/acc.pdf#page=129"} exercise 7H
              of (
              %a{:href => "#AdamekHerrlichStrecker"}> AdamekHerrlichStrecker
              ). It is however nonconstructive (because it contains if-then-else lines); for a constructive proof, see
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp#eq"} here
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \hookrightarrow H
              be a subgroup. We need to define another group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and group homomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1, f_2 : H \to G
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K = \{h \in H  | f_1(h) = f_2(h)\}
                    \\,.
            %p To that end, let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi h
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X  := H/K  \coprod  \{\hat K\}  := \{ h K | h \in H \}  \coprod  \{\hat K\}
            %p
              be the set of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat K
            %p Let then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G = Aut_{Set}(X)
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+group"} permutation group
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \in G
              to be the permutation that exchanges the coset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e K
              with the extra element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat K
              and is the identity on all other elements.
            %p
              Finally define group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1,f_2 : H \to G
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi h
                              %mi h
                              %mo ′
                              %mi K
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mi h
                              %mo ′
                              %mi K
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi K
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi x
                              %mo =
                              %mover
                                %mi K
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_1(h) : x \mapsto
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    h h' K &amp; if x = h' K
                    \\\
                    \\hat K &amp; if x = \hat K
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_2(h) = \rho \circ f_1(h) \circ \rho^{-1}
                    \\,.
            %p It is clear that these maps are indeed group homomorphisms.
            %p
              So for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in H
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_1(h) : \hat K \mapsto \hat K
                    \\,,
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi e
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi h
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_1(h) : e K \mapsto h K
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi e
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi h
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mi K
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mi h
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi K
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi h
                              %mi K
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_2(h)
                    \:
                    \\hat K
                    \\mapsto
                    e K
                    \\mapsto
                    h K
                    \\mapsto
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\hat K &amp; if h \in K
                    \\\
                    h K &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi e
                    %mi K
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ↦
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi e
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_2(h) : e K \mapsto \hat K \mapsto \hat K \mapsto e K
                    \\,.
            %p
              So we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1(h) = f_2(h)
              precisely if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in K
          %h2#Infty1Version
            In an
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \stackrel{f}{\to} d \stackrel{\to}{\to} e
            may be thought of as the beginning of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            diagram over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial
            diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 0
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c \stackrel{f}{\to} d_0 \stackrel{\to}{\to} d_1
                  \\stackrel{\to}{\stackrel{\to}{\to}}
                  d_2
                  \\cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            Accordingly, it is not unreasonable to define a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} regular monomorphism in an (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} limit in a quasi-category
            of a cosimplicial diagram.
          %p
            In practice this is of particular relevance for the
            = succeed "-version" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : c \to d
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            if for all objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in C
            the induced morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : C(d,e) \to C(c,e)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular monomorphism
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (for instance
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} modeled
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            over a cosimplicial diagram in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
          %p
            %strong Warning.
            The same warning as at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
            applies: with this definition of regular monomorphism in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            these may fail to satisfy various definitions of plain monomorphisms that one might think of.
